  "reason": "The strongest evidence so far is RNA-only multiprofile scvi_n200 with transformer aggregation (config_006, 0.653 accuracy / 0.628 F1), while image-only models are weak, with imagenet_vit_l slightly ahead of resnet50. The key uncertainty is whether image features provide complementary signal when fused with the best RNA representation. config_038 keeps the best RNA encoder, multiprofile setting, and transformer aggregation, and adds the stronger image encoder with simple concat fusion, directly testing whether multimodal fusion can improve over the RNA-only baseline. This is the best next experiment because it exploits the strongest RNA evidence while resolving whether the image modality is worth further investment before testing more complex fusion variants."
